The migration from ethers v5 to v6 changed how amounts are represented. v5 used BigNumber objects. v6 uses native BigInt. Most codebases updated the obvious call sites and missed the ones inside utility functions.

This fails silently in development and throws in production:

const GAS_LIMIT = 21000; // number, not BigInt

const tx = await wallet.sendTransaction({
  to: recipient,
  value: parseEther(amount),
  gasLimit: GAS_LIMIT, // passes type checks, throws at runtime
});

